mod backend.compiler.expressions.primary;

/**
 * PRIMARY EXPRESSIONS: names and what hangs off them
 *
 *      total           a plain name                    identifier_expression.sharp
 *      std.io#name     a name in a named module        module_name_expression.sharp
 *      self   base     the object itself               self_expression.sharp
 *      a.b   a->b      a member of a value or class    the package below this one: primary/members
 *      a?.b  a!!.b     ... of a value that may be null (member_expression.sharp, safe_navigation.sharp ...)
 *
 * and the three pieces they share:
 *
 *      found_names.sharp   what name lookup found -> the typed-tree node for it
 *      field_access.sharp  reading a field: static or not, through its getter or not, its type
 *      named_types.sharp   a class name written in an expression (`list<int>`) -> its resolved type
 *
 * The files of this package (module `backend.compiler.expressions.primary`)
 * are the six named above plus this front door. The lookups themselves are
 * in backend/compiler/names; this package turns their answers into tree
 * nodes and checks the rules of USING a name (static against instance,
 * access, null safety).
 *
 *      C++ comparison: compiler/expressions/primary/ (dotted_identifier,
 *      self, base ...) and `resolve_normal_item` / `resolve_field` in
 *      dependency.cpp, which do lookup and code generation in one step.
 */
